column2:
May Keshava protect in front, the discus-bearer, bright as Jambu gold; behind, Narayana with the conch, like a dark-blue cloud;
naradapuran:70:120	above, Madhava with the mace, dark as a blue lotus; on the right, Govinda with the bow, great and bright as the moon;
naradapuran:70:121	on the north, Vishnu with the plough, like a lotus filament; in the south-east, Madhusudana with the pestle, lotus-eyed;
naradapuran:70:122	in the south-west, Trivikrama with the sword, bright as fire; in the north-west, Madhava with the thunderbolt, bright as the young sun;
naradapuran:70:123	in the north-east, the lotus-eyed Shridhara with the pattisha; above, Hrishikesha with the mudgara, bright as lightning;
naradapuran:70:124	below, Padmanabha, bright as a thousand suns, with all weapons, all power, the primal of all, facing all directions;
naradapuran:70:125	bright as Indra-gopa insect, may the unconquered with noose in hand protect; may Hari Damodara protect the body inside and out.
naradapuran:70:126	Thus everywhere is the flawless cage of twelve": I have entered it, and I have no fear whatever."
